uns` both report ci-0001 as passed on this branch's commit.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 385672, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VsHu6rpegnAfvH9Mg6npXe", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 385672, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VsHu6rpegnAfvH9Mg6npXe", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 391765, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why the test failed.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on my commit (`08d3cd5986`). The first time I waited for the result, the CI tool reported a failure, but that report described a different branch and commit (main, `0c0ffee000`) and a test file, `tests/test_ledger.py`, that isn't in this repo. Checking the run directly, two ways, both showed it passed on my commit, so I went ahead with the PR. I noted this in the PR description in case the CI tooling is worth a look.\n\nI haven't merged it. That needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0147Hwarseswrsu5M4Gq1HBE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": 